{
  "description": "A regex key that isn't valid is REGEX_ERROR (Format 7.2, 14, 15.3): one that doesn't compile, one with a form outside the shared syntax, such as an inline flag, a lookahead or a backreference, one with a flag other than i, m and s or a repeated flag, one nesting groups more than 100 deep, and one longer than 1000 bytes written out in full. A key with text after its last slash that isn't flags is a plain key",
  "note": "Written out, (a{10}){n} is (aaaaaaaaaa) n times, 12n bytes: 996 for n = 83, 1008 for 84 and 2400 for 200. a{n,} is n copies of a then a*, n + 2 bytes: 1000 for n = 998, 1001 for 999. The slashes around a key aren't part of its pattern.",
